## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design cross-region routing with an external layer, ensuring hot tenants get low-latency reads even during failover. Evaluates data freshness guarantees, cache invalidation, and security controls.

## Key Concepts
- Aurora Global Database lag and cross-region read consistency
- External routing layer for per-tenant decisions
- Regional caches with TTL-based freshness and invalidation
- DR drills: staged failover, latency validation, and monitoring
- Security: IAM roles, KMS, network segmentation, least privilege

## Code Example
```javascript
function routeTenant(tenantId, region) {
  const isHot = checkTenantHot(tenantId);
  if (isHot && region === nearestHotRegion(tenantId)) {
    return { endpoint: 'regional-cache', cacheHint: true };
  }
  return { endpoint: 'primary-read-replica', cacheHint: false };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate cache coherence across regions during burst traffic?
- Which metrics would you instrument to detect SLAs violations in real time?
- How would you handle tenant onboarding/offboarding affecting routing rules?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical use of IAM DB authentication, RDS Proxy, and fine-grained access controls across accounts, plus a concrete testing plan.

## Key Concepts
- IAM database authentication with Aurora PostgreSQL
- RDS Proxy for serverless/large-concurrency access
- Fine-grained grants and per-service DB users
- Cross-account role mappings and network isolation
- Validation: latency, authorization, and failover tests

## Code Example
```sql
CREATE USER sales_read LOGIN;
GRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA sales TO sales_read;
GRANT SELECT ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA sales TO sales_read;

CREATE USER orders_rw LOGIN;
GRANT INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA orders TO orders_rw;
GRANT SELECT ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA orders TO orders_rw;
ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES IN SCHEMA orders GRANT INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE ON TABLES TO orders_rw;
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify IAM role to DB user mapping using Lambda? 
- What monitoring would you set to detect privilege drift or misconfiguration?

